7-18T04:08:15.342Z","score":11,"matchedTerms":["canada"],"summary":"<p>Video <a href=\"https://x.com/solmamakwa/status/2077164640790892548\">footage of a train</a> near the community of Armstrong, Ontario, highlights the speed and ferocity of one of more than 100 wildfires currently burning in Canada. 'This could potentially overtake us here â€¦ This has gotten a little scary,' says a crew member as a wall of flames whips across the windows. 'Weâ€™re encased in flames now.' The railway company Canadian National confirmed the crew has been 'safely evacuated' from the area</p><p></p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/jul/15/wildfires-in-ontario-make-toronto-canada-air-quality-worst-in-world\">Wildfires in Ontario make Toronto air quality wo..."},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.source","subject":"a-bay-area-financial-analyst-wants-a-piece-of-this-mineral-rich-seabed-surrounded-by-3-pacific-nations","wire":"environment","path":"/home/emsenn/info/lib/emsenn/services/561-group/services/rsc-quiescent/services/koios-news/sites/koios.news/store/environment/a-bay-area-financial-analyst-wants-a-piece-of-this-mineral-rich-seabed-surrounded-by-3-pacific-nations.json","title":"A Bay Area financial analyst wants a piece of this mineral-rich seabed surrounded by 3 Pacific nations","url":"https://grist.org/oceans/american-deep-sea-minerals-application-pacific-island-fisheries/","domain":"grist.org","published":"Wed, 15 Jul 2026 08:30:00 +0000","assertedAt":"2026-07-18T04:08:15.342Z","score":11,"matchedTerms":["nations"],"summary":"Last summer, at the United Nations Ocean Conference, French Polynesia established the worldâ€™s largest contiguous marine protected area, reinforcing its 2022 ban on seabed mining. â€œThe deep sea is not for sale,â€ Franceâ€™s president, Emmanuel Macron, said at the time.&nbsp; A year later, that might not hold true for the waters just beyond French Polynesiaâ€™s maritime border. A little-known American startup is seeking the Trump administrationâ€™s approval to lease 25 million acres of international waters for mining exploration just outside the areas over which French Polynesia, the Cook Islands, and Kiribati have exclusive rights. The area, called Eastern High Seas Pocket 3 because it is entirel..."}],"claims":[{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.claim","sourceSubject":"thousands-flee-as-first-nations-bear-the-brunt-of-canada-s-wildfires","sourceUrl":"https://grist.org/indigenous/thousands-flee-as-first-nations-bear-the-brunt-of-canadas-wildfires/","id":"title","predicate":"title","object":"Thousands flee as First Nations bear the brunt of Canadaâ€™s wildfires","force":"alleges","status":"supported","assertedAt":"2026-07-18T04:08:15.342Z"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.claim","sourceSubject":"thousands-flee-as-first-nations-bear-the-brunt-of-canada-s-wildfires","sourceUrl":"https://grist.org/indigenous/thousands-flee-as-first-nations-bear-the-brunt-of-canadas-wildfires/","id":"url","predicate":"url","object":"https://grist.org/indigenous/thousands-flee-as-first-nations-bear-the-brunt-of-canadas-wildfires/","force":"alleges","status":"supported","assertedAt":"2026-07-18T04:08:15.342Z"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.claim","sourceSubject":"thousands-flee-as-first-nations-bear-the-brunt-of-canada-s-wildfires","sourceUrl":"https://grist.org/indigenous/thousands-flee-as-first-nations-bear-the-brunt-of-canadas-wildfires/","id":"summary","predicate":"summary","object":"More than 900 wildfires are burning throughout Canada, with devastating impacts for First Nations. Thirteen Nations remain under evacuation orders that have forced 2,182 people from their homes.&nbsp; The Namaygoosisagagun (Collins) First Nation watched one blaze largely destroy its entire community in less than an hour, forcing residents to flee by boat. Residents reported having only minutes to gather their belongings before homes were overtaken by the flames on Wednesday, and Anishinabek Nation Grand Council Chief Linda Debassige said in a statement that all community members have been accounted for pending a full assessment. â€œIt is with heartfelt sadness that I share that our member First Nation, Namaygoosisagagun First Nation, has been devastated by an unexpected and fast-moving wildfire that advanced toward and through the community, causing extensive damage and destruction to homes and community buildings,â€ Debassige said in the statement. Of the 903 fires burning as of Friday , 750 remained out of control and 43 had started within the prior 24 hours.&nbsp; The effect has been greatest in Ontario, where seven First Nations have fled the 193 fires now burning there. According to the Chiefs of Ontario, several communities were cleared under mandatory orders issued by their leadership with support from the Ontario Provincial Police. In addition to Namaygoosisagagun, Whitesand First Nation, Kiashke Zaaging Anishinaabek, and Animbiigoo Zaagiâ€™igan Anishinaabek are among those impacted by those orders. Dozens of non-Indigenous communities throughout the province have been ordered to evacuate as well. The Namaygoosisagagun (Collins) First Nation is about 125 miles north of Thunder Bay and inaccessible by road. Debassige told The Canadian Press that residents did not receive advance warning from provincial or national officials, nor did they receive any evacuation support. Itâ€™s been reported that community members went â€‹door-to-door warning their neighbors, and more than two dozen people fled by boat just as the flames approached. Meaghan Daniel, a lawyer who represents Collins First Nation, told The Canadian Press that residents also are being denied assistance because the national government does not recognize it as a First Nation. Although residents are recognized as First Nations people under the Indian Act, the community itself is not. Its leaders have long sought official recognition. Daniel sent a letter to Mandy Gull-Masty, the Indigenous Services minister calling on the agency to provide the emergency, recovery, and reconstruction support recognized communities are entitled to. â€œTo be clear, if Namaygoosisagagun is denied access to the emergency and rebuilding supports available to recognized First Nations, it will not simply suffer a slower recovery. It may lose forever the opportunity to rebuild the community its members spent decades creating,â€ the letter states, according to The Canadian Press . â€œIn those circumstances, the question is not merely whether recovery will be delayed. It is whether Namaygoosisagagun will have a future in the place it has called home since time immemorial.â€ Read Next A â€˜crisis communication gapâ€™ threatens Indigenous peoples Dionne Phillips In a statement emailed to The Canadian Press, Eric Head, a spokesperson for the agency, said efforts are now underway to determine the communityâ€™s immediate needs and coordinate support to meet them. As the situation unfolds, many other First Nations are currently undergoing the processes required to declare states of emergency and evacuate their communities. Ontario Chiefs held an emergency meeting Wednesday and expressed frustration with the bureaucratic processes in place to access emergency response services as well as a lack of communication from government officials regarding practices in place to declare a state of emergency. â€œJurisdictional disputes and administrative delays have immediate consequences and put lives at risk,â€ said Ontario Regional Chief Abram Benedict. â€œThe priority of our leadership is to get people out as quickly and safely as possible. This needs to be everyoneâ€™s priority rather than financial discussions and technicalities.â€ Benedict added that people are coming together to help one another.&nbsp; â€œWe are on the front lines of this catastrophe that is having international impacts. Our First Nations leadership, emergency responders, and community members are working to protect their people and homelands,â€ Benedict said. On Thursday, during its national assembly in Ottawa, the Assembly of First Nations passed emergency resolutions to provide support for Namaygoosisagagun and other impacted First Nations. It also called on the federal government to provide ongoing support throughout the crisis. The Anishinabek Nation asked for prayers for the people of the community that are dealing with this unprecedented loss.&nbsp; â€œWe ask that you please keep Chief Paavola, the citizens of Namaygoosisagagun First Nation, and all those affected by these wildfires in your prayers, and give them the privacy, time, and space required as they navigate this devastating situation,â€ the Nation said in a statement. â€œWe send our heartfelt condolences, and our thoughts are with Namaygoosisagagun members who have suffered this tremendous loss of their entire community; our Anishinabek Nation family will be with you.â€&nbsp; Grist provided additional information for this story. This story was originally published by Grist with the headline Thousands flee as First Nations bear the brunt of Canadaâ€™s wildfires on Jul 17, 2026.","force":"alleges","status":"supported","assertedAt":"2026-07-18T04:08:15.342Z"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.claim","sourceSubject":"thousands-flee-as-first-nations-bear-the-brunt-of-canada-s-wildfires","sourceUrl":"https://grist.org/indigenous/thousands-flee-as-first-nations-bear-the-brunt-of-canadas-wildfires/","id":"published","predicate":"published","object":"Fri, 17 Jul 2026 20:48:10 +0000","force":"alleges","status":"supported","assertedAt":"2026-07-18T04:08:15.342Z"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.claim","sourceSubject":"eight-facts-about-air-conditioning-amid-an-overheated-global-debate","sourceUrl":"https://www.carbonbrief.org/eight-facts-about-air-conditioning-amid-an-overheated-global-debate/","id":"title","predicate":"title","object":"Eight facts about air conditioning amid an overheated global debate","force":"alleges","status":"supported","assertedAt":"2026-07-18T04:08:15.342Z"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.claim","sourceSubject":"eight-facts-about-air-conditioning-amid-an-overheated-global-debate","sourceUrl":"https://www.carbonbrief.org/eight-facts-about-air-conditioning-amid-an-overheated-global-debate/","id":"url","predicate":"url","object":"https://www.carbonbrief.org/eight-facts-about-air-conditioning-amid-an-overheated-global-debate/","force":"alleges","status":"supported","assertedAt":"2026-07-18T04:08:15.342Z"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.claim","sourceSubject":"eight-facts-about-air-conditioning-amid-an-overheated-global-debate","sourceUrl":"https://www.carbonbrief.org/eight-facts-about-air-conditioning-amid-an-overheated-global-debate/","id":"summary","predicate":"summary","object":"As successive heatwaves hit Europe, air-conditioning (AC) has emerged as a new front in the international â€œ culture war â€ over climate action. France, Germany and the UK have experienced record-breaking heat and thousands of heat-related deaths this summer, with June temperatures in many regions passing 40C. This has drawn attention to the relatively low rates of AC use in these countries â€“ and in Europe as a whole â€“ especially when compared to its widespread adoption in the US. Legacy newspapers , bloggers and even Elon Musk have all weighed in on â€œ European hostility â€ to AC, criticising Europeâ€™s â€œ cultural conservatism â€ and â€œ overbearing governments â€. Right-wing politicians, including National Rally in France and the UK Conservatives , have styled themselves as champions of AC, while opposing efforts to tackle climate change. Missing from most of these interventions is the fact that human-caused climate change has made once-rare heat far more common, in what is the worldâ€™s fastest warming continent . Carbon Brief analysis for this article shows that, until the 2020s, it was rare for many European cities to see days above 30C, making AC an unnecessary expense. Here, Carbon B...","force":"alleges","status":"supported","assertedAt":"2026-07-18T04:08:15.342Z"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.claim","sourceSubject":"eight-facts-about-air-conditioning-amid-an-overheated-global-debate","sourceUrl":"https://www.carbonbrief.org/eight-facts-about-air-conditioning-amid-an-overheated-global-debate/","id":"published","predicate":"published","object":"Fri, 10 Jul 2026 14:21:15 +0000","force":"alleges","status":"supported","assertedAt":"2026-07-18T04:08:15.342Z"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.claim","sourceSubject":"train-crew-in-canada-encased-by-intense-flames-amid-wildfires-video","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/video/2026/jul/16/train-crew-in-canada-encased-by-intense-flames-amid-wildfires-video","id":"title","predicate":"title","object":"Train crew in Canada 'encased' by intense flames amid wildfires - video","force":"alleges","status":"supported","assertedAt":"2026-07-18T04:08:15.342Z"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.claim","sourceSubject":"train-crew-in-canada-encased-by-intense-flames-amid-wildfires-video","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/video/2026/jul/16/train-crew-in-canada-encased-by-intense-flames-amid-wildfires-video","id":"url","predicate":"url","object":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/video/2026/jul/16/train-crew-in-canada-encased-by-intense-flames-amid-wildfires-video","force":"alleges","status":"supported","assertedAt":"2026-07-18T04:08:15.342Z"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.claim","sourceSubject":"train-crew-in-canada-encased-by-intense-flames-amid-wildfires-video","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/video/2026/jul/16/train-crew-in-canada-encased-by-intense-flames-amid-wildfires-video","id":"summary","predicate":"summary","object":"<p>Video <a href=\"https://x.com/solmamakwa/status/2077164640790892548\">footage of a train</a> near the community of Armstrong, Ontario, highlights the speed and ferocity of one of more than 100 wildfires currently burning in Canada. 'This could potentially overtake us here â€¦ This has gotten a little scary,' says a crew member as a wall of flames whips across the windows. 'Weâ€™re encased in flames now.' The railway company Canadian National confirmed the crew has been 'safely evacuated' from the area</p><p></p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/jul/15/wildfires-in-ontario-make-toronto-canada-air-quality-worst-in-world\">Wildfires in Ontario make Toronto air quality worst in world</a></p></li></ul> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/video/2026/jul/16/train-crew-in-canada-encased-by-intense-flames-amid-wildfires-video\">Continue reading...</a>","force":"alleges","status":"supported","assertedAt":"2026-07-18T04:08:15.342Z"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.claim","sourceSubject":"train-crew-in-canada-encased-by-intense-flames-amid-wildfires-video","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/video/2026/jul/16/train-crew-in-canada-encased-by-intense-flames-amid-wildfires-video","id":"published","predicate":"published","object":"Thu, 16 Jul 2026 01:37:13 GMT","force":"alleges","status":"supported","assertedAt":"2026-07-18T04:08:15.342Z"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.claim","sourceSubject":"a-bay-area-financial-analyst-wants-a-piece-of-this-mineral-rich-seabed-surrounded-by-3-pacific-nations","sourceUrl":"https://grist.org/oceans/american-deep-sea-minerals-application-pacific-island-fisheries/","id":"title","predicate":"title","object":"A Bay Area financial analyst wants a piece of this mineral-rich seabed surrounded by 3 Pacific nations","force":"alleges","status":"supported","assertedAt":"2026-07-18T04:08:15.342Z"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.claim","sourceSubject":"a-bay-area-financial-analyst-wants-a-piece-of-this-mineral-rich-seabed-surrounded-by-3-pacific-nations","sourceUrl":"https://grist.org/oceans/american-deep-sea-minerals-application-pacific-island-fisheries/","id":"url","predicate":"url","object":"https://grist.org/oceans/american-deep-sea-minerals-application-pacific-island-fisheries/","force":"alleges","status":"supported","assertedAt":"2026-07-18T04:08:15.342Z"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.claim","sourceSubject":"a-bay-area-financial-analyst-wants-a-piece-of-this-mineral-rich-seabed-surrounded-by-3-pacific-nations","sourceUrl":"https://grist.org/oceans/american-deep-sea-minerals-application-pacific-island-fisheries/","id":"summary","predicate":"summary","object":"Last summer, at the United Nations Ocean Conference, French Polynesia established the worldâ€™s largest contiguous marine protected area, reinforcing its 2022 ban on seabed mining. â€œThe deep sea is not for sale,â€ Franceâ€™s president, Emmanuel Macron, said at the time.&nbsp; A year later, that might not hold true for the waters just beyond French Polynesiaâ€™s maritime border. A little-known American startup is seeking the Trump administrationâ€™s approval to lease 25 million acres of international waters for mining exploration just outside the areas over which French Polynesia, the Cook Islands, and Kiribati have exclusive rights. The area, called Eastern High Seas Pocket 3 because it is entirely surrounded by waters known as the exclusive economic zones of the three nations, has an abundance of albacore, yellowfin, and bigeye tuna and is visited by dozens of fishing vessels each year.&nbsp; American Deep Sea Minerals is the first company to propose exploring the seabed there for manganese and other critical minerals, part of a global rush to capitalize on the essential components of batteries, military technologies, and other modern technologies. Read Next A guide to the 4 minerals sh...","force":"alleges","status":"supported","assertedAt":"2026-07-18T04:08:15.342Z"},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.claim","sourceSubject":"a-bay-area-financial-analyst-wants-a-piece-of-this-mineral-rich-seabed-surrounded-by-3-pacific-nations","sourceUrl":"https://grist.org/oceans/american-deep-sea-minerals-application-pacific-island-fisheries/","id":"published","predicate":"published","object":"Wed, 15 Jul 2026 08:30:00 +0000","force":"alleges","status":"supported","assertedAt":"2026-07-18T04:08:15.342Z"}],"warrant":{"status":"research-intake","supportClaimCount":16,"refutationClaimCount":0,"uncertainClaimCount":0,"sourceDomainCount":3,"sourceDomains":["grist.org","carbonbrief.org","theguardian.com"],"note":"This warrant is source-bound research intake. Writing may cite these records, but only editing and publishing gates can settle a manuscript."},"editorialRisks":[{"code":"demand-is-not-evidence","severity":"note","message":"The term and beat justify research attention only; they do not support any factual claim."}],"sourceUrls":["https://grist.org/indigenous/thousands-flee-as-first-nations-bear-the-brunt-of-canadas-wildfires/","https://www.carbonbrief.org/eight-facts-about-air-conditioning-amid-an-overheated-global-debate/","https://www.theguardian.com/world/video/2026/jul/16/train-crew-in-canada-encased-by-intense-flames-amid-wildfires-video","https://grist.org/oceans/american-deep-sea-minerals-application-pacific-island-fisheries/"],"candidateReferences":[{"id":"grist-org-be22bafe","type":"webpage","title":"Thousands flee as First Nations bear the brunt of Canadaâ€™s wildfires","URL":"https://grist.org/indigenous/thousands-flee-as-first-nations-bear-the-brunt-of-canadas-wildfires/","container-title":"grist.org","issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,17]]}},{"id":"carbonbrief-org-6941adb8","type":"webpage","title":"Eight facts about air conditioning amid an overheated global debate","URL":"https://www.carbonbrief.org/eight-facts-about-air-conditioning-amid-an-overheated-global-debate/","container-title":"carbonbrief.org","issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,10]]}},{"id":"theguardian-com-90d8b48c","type":"webpage","title":"Train crew in Canada 'encased' by intense flames amid wildfires - video","URL":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/video/2026/jul/16/train-crew-in-canada-encased-by-intense-flames-amid-wildfires-video","container-title":"theguardian.com","issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,16]]}},{"id":"grist-org-1fc69e3a","type":"webpage","title":"A Bay Area financial analyst wants a piece of this mineral-rich seabed surrounded by 3 Pacific nations","URL":"https://grist.org/oceans/american-deep-sea-minerals-application-pacific-island-fisheries/","container-title":"grist.org","issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,7,15]]}}],"context":["[1] Thousands flee as First Nations bear the brunt of Canadaâ€™s wildfires (grist.org, Fri, 17 Jul 2026 20:48:10 +0000) - More than 900 wildfires are burning throughout Canada, with devastating impacts for First Nations. Thirteen Nations remain under evacuation orders that have forced 2,182 people from their homes.&nbsp; The Namaygoosisagagun (Collins) First Nation watched one blaze largely destroy its entire community in less than an hour, forcing residents to flee by boat. Residents reported having only minutes to gather their belongings before homes were overtaken by the flames on Wednesday, and Anishinabek Nation Grand Council Chief Linda Debassige said in a statement that all community members have been accounted for pending a full assessment. â€œIt is with heartfelt sadness that I share that our member F...","[2] Eight facts about air conditioning amid an overheated global debate (carbonbrief.org, Fri, 10 Jul 2026 14:21:15 +0000) - As successive heatwaves hit Europe, air-conditioning (AC) has emerged as a new front in the international â€œ culture war â€ over climate action. France, Germany and the UK have experienced record-breaking heat and thousands of heat-related deaths this summer, with June temperatures in many regions passing 40C. This has drawn attention to the relatively low rates of AC use in these countries â€“ and in Europe as a whole â€“ especially when compared to its widespread adoption in the US. Legacy newspapers , bloggers and even Elon Musk have all weighed in on â€œ European hostility â€ to AC, criticising Europeâ€™s â€œ cultural conservatism â€ and â€œ overbearing governments â€. Right-wing politicians, includin...","[3] Train crew in Canada 'encased' by intense flames amid wildfires - video (theguardian.com, Thu, 16 Jul 2026 01:37:13 GMT) - <p>Video <a href=\"https://x.com/solmamakwa/status/2077164640790892548\">footage of a train</a> near the community of Armstrong, Ontario, highlights the speed and ferocity of one of more than 100 wildfires currently burning in Canada. 'This could potentially overtake us here â€¦ This has gotten a little scary,' says a crew member as a wall of flames whips across the windows. 'Weâ€™re encased in flames now.' The railway company Canadian National confirmed the crew has been 'safely evacuated' from the area</p><p></p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/jul/15/wildfires-in-ontario-make-toronto-canada-air-quality-worst-in-world\">Wildfires in Ontario make Toronto air quality wo...","[4] A Bay Area financial analyst wants a piece of this mineral-rich seabed surrounded by 3 Pacific nations (grist.org, Wed, 15 Jul 2026 08:30:00 +0000) - Last summer, at the United Nations Ocean Conference, French Polynesia established the worldâ€™s largest contiguous marine protected area, reinforcing its 2022 ban on seabed mining. â€œThe deep sea is not for sale,â€ Franceâ€™s president, Emmanuel Macron, said at the time.&nbsp; A year later, that might not hold true for the waters just beyond French Polynesiaâ€™s maritime border. A little-known American startup is seeking the Trump administrationâ€™s approval to lease 25 million acres of international waters for mining exploration just outside the areas over which French Polynesia, the Cook Islands, and Kiribati have exclusive rights. The area, called Eastern High Seas Pocket 3 because it is entirel..."],"accountableAttention":{"rule":"make-the-click-preserve-the-warrant","headlineMustPreserve":["attribution","modality","scope","uncertainty","correction state"],"forbiddenStrengthenings":["source claim to newsroom fact","may/could/alleged to does/did/proves","single case to trend","correlation to causation","reader demand to evidence"],"correctionSurfacePolicy":"Any later correction to a cited claim must be propagated to body copy, headline, social cards, feeds, JSON-LD, and syndicated packets."},"constraints":["This packet is research intake, not a publishable article.","sourceUrls are source material; candidateReferences are the CSL-shaped cited cut available to writing.","claims remain attributed and source-bound until a manuscript's editing and publishing gates settle them.","Attention surfaces may increase curiosity, but must not create factual commitments absent from the packet or manuscript references.","Publication still requires body citations, editing standards review, and an explicit publishing action."]}}]

